    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>Founded by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sargon-of-akkad">Sargon of Akkad</a>, it is widely regarded as the world's first empire, uniting the Sumerian city-states under one ruler.</li><li>Its governors, standard measures and written Akkadian set the template that later Mesopotamian empires followed.</li><li>Gutian raids, palace murders and a severe drought around 2200 BCE brought it down; its capital has never been found.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sargon-of-akkad">Sargon</a>'s daughter <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/enheduanna">Enheduanna</a>, high priestess of the moon god at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ur">Ur</a>, is often described as the first named author in recorded history.</p></aside>
